    "ImageDescription": {
      "value": "Another in a three part series of homes I took footage for in Sept-Oct 2019. This is another of my Uncles homes in Addison, VT. I love how the colors pop in this footage, looks more real than in person!  Here you get some good panoramic shots of the surrounding Vermont landscape. As opposed to the other footage by the lake, this was much more 'fun' to fly since there wasn't the worries of hitting all those trees or crashing to a watery end. \n<p>I put the drone in sport mode for the shots where we fly down to the back edge of the property and back, we hit 40+mph on that shot as well. I am attempting to be more smooth in my transitions, such as the 360 around the home, but I really feel this needs more work. \n</p><p>The footage took very little editing, since the first take was pretty spot on, but I did experiment with adding graphics (title/credit/etc) and some music track to keep it a bit more interesting.\n</p>\nHope you enjoy.",
      "source": "commons-desc-page"
    },
